{
 "title": "Geometry nodes 3: a fence along curves",
 "summary": "A fence piece modelled from cubes (a post and two rails) with a wood material (a stretched noise on its UVs through a brown ramp, bump, rough), then Geometry Nodes on a Bezier curve: Resample Curve by length, Delete Geometry with a random boolean selection (probability 0.15) for missing pieces, Instance on Points with the piece from Object Info, aligned to the curve by Align Euler to Vector on the Curve Tangent. Drawing more curves draws more fence: a winding run, a short run and (beyond the tutorial) a closed square pen.",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "FenceLine",
   "description": "the fences"
  }
 ],
